,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作词: \"},{\"tx\":\"Don Henley\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Glenn Frey\"}]}\n{\"t\":1000,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作曲: \"},{\"tx\":\"Don Henley\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Glenn Frey\"}]}\n{\"t\":2000,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"制作人: \"},{\"tx\":\"Bill Szymczyk\"}]}\n[00:10.110]She came from Providence\n[00:13.940]The one in Rhode Island\n[00:17.700]Where the old world shadows hang\n[00:21.470]Heavy in the air\n[00:24.920]She packed her hopes and dreams\n[00:28.680]Like a refugee\n[00:32.450]Just as her father came across the sea\n[00:41.770]She heard about a place people were smiling\n[00:49.270]They spoke about the red man\'s way\n[00:52.540]And how they loved the land\n[00:56.580]And they came from everywhere\n[01:00.410]To the Great Divide\n[01:04.210]Seeking a place to stand\n[01:07.720]Or a place to hide\n[01:13.770]Down in the crowded bars\n[01:16.880]Out for a good time\n[01:21.080]Can\'t wait to tell you all\n[01:24.660]What it\'s like up there\n[01:28.640]And they called it paradise\n[01:32.440]I don\'t know why\n[01:36.010]Somebody laid the mountains low\n[01:40.340]While the town got high\n[02:08.280]Then the chilly winds blew down\n[02:12.610]Across the desert\n[02:16.410]Through the canyons of the coast,\n[02:20.060]To the Malibu\n[02:23.820]Where the pretty people play,\n[02:27.740]Hungry for power\n[02:31.570]To light their neon way\n[02:35.430]And give them things to do\n[02:41.010]Some rich men came and raped the land,\n[02:44.610]Nobody caught them\n[02:48.430]Put up a bunch of ugly boxes, and Jesus,\n[02:52.890]People bought them\n[02:56.230]And they called it paradise\n[02:59.840]The place to be\n[03:03.700]They watched the hazy sun, sinking in the sea\n[04:20.630]You can leave it all behind\n[04:24.410]And sail to Lahaina\n[04:28.290]Just like the missionaries did, so many years ago\n[04:36.030]They even brought a neon sign:\"Jesus is coming\"\n[04:43.680]Brought the white man\'s burden down\n[04:47.580]Brought the white man\'s reign\n[04:51.600]Who will provide the grand design?\n[04:55.150]What is yours and what is mine?\n[04:59.150]Cause there is no more new frontier\n[05:03.220]We have got to make it here\n[05:07.170]We satifsy our endless needs\n[05:10.980]And justify our bloody deeds,\n[05:14.490]In the name of destiny\n[05:18.570]And the name of God\n[05:24.220]And you can see them there,\n[05:27.860]On Sunday morning\n[05:31.680]Stand up and sing about\n[05:35.260]What it\'s like up there\n[05:39.320]They call it paradise\n[05:42.330]I don\'t know why\n[05:45.560]You call someplace paradise,\n[05:50.300]Kiss it goodbye','448.78','原声带,欧美流行','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songCovers/ca9cfd42-d27d-4d5b-bf9e-4516991503aa-Eagles-The Last Resort (2013 Remaster).jpg','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songs/449592a8-ca4d-42a1-b6f6-3a95837418e0-Eagles - The Last Resort (2013 Remaster).mp3','2026-04-16'),(634,155,'The Sad Cafe (2013 Remaster)','The Studio Albums 1972-1979 (2013 Remaster)','{\"t\":0,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作词: \"},{\"tx\":\"J. D. Souther\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Joe Walsh\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Don Henley\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Glenn Frey\"}]}\n{\"t\":1000,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作曲: \"},{\"tx\":\"J. D. Souther\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Joe Walsh\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Don Henley\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Glenn Frey\"}]}\n[00:38.699]Out in the shiny night the rain was softly falling\n[00:47.989]The tracks that ran down the boulevard had\n[00:52.349]all been washed away\n[00:59.199]Out of the silver light the past came softly calling\n[01:07.190]And I remember the times we spent\n[01:11.500]inside the Sad Cafe\n[01:19.130]Oh it seemed like a holy place\n[01:23.900]protected by amazing grace\n[01:28.830]And we would sing right out loud the\n[01:32.320]things we could not say\n[01:38.289]We thought we could change this world\n[01:41.780]with words like \"love\" and \"freedom\"\n[01:47.220]We were part of the lonely crowd\n[01:50.960]Inside the Sad Cafe\n[01:56.700]Oh, expecting to fly,\n[02:04.780]we would meet on that beautiful shore in the sweet by and by\n[02:15.870]Some of their dreams came true,\n[02:19.490]some just passed away\n[02:24.480]And some of the stayed behind\n[02:28.510]inside the Sad Cafe.\n[02:52.200]The clouds rolled in and hid that shore\n[03:01.800]Now that Glory Train, it don\'t stop here no more\n[03:10.930]Now I look at the years gone by,\n[03:15.420]and wonder at the powers that be.\n[03:20.179]I don\'t know why fortune smiles on some\n[03:24.950]and let\'s the rest go free\n[03:30.920]Maybe the time has drawn the faces I recall\n[03:39.380]But things in this life change very slowly,\n[03:43.310]if they ever change at all\n[03:49.540]There\'s no use in asking why,\n[03:52.820]it just turned out that way\n[03:58.560]So meet me at midnight baby\n[04:02.380]inside the Sad Cafe.\n[04:07.510]Why don\'t you meet me at midnight baby,\n[04:12.100]inside the Sad Cafe.\n[05:03.360]','332.98','欧美流行','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songCovers/40cc70f6-7251-4f26-b836-a092e583ef39-Eagles-The Sad Cafe (2013 Remaster).jpg','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songs/a14e2772-7e11-4f38-b8a4-c47e03a81df3-Eagles - The Sad Cafe (2013 Remaster).mp3','2026-04-16'),(635,155,'Try and Love Again (2013 Remaster)','Hotel California (2013 Remaster)','{\"t\":0,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作词: \"},{\"tx\":\"Randy Meisner\"}]}\n{\"t\":1000,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作曲: \"},{\"tx\":\"Randy Meisner\"}]}\n[00:26.43]When you\'re out there on your own\n[00:30.81]Where your memories can find you\n[00:33.68]\n[00:37.06]Like a circle goes around\n[00:40.18]You were lost until you found out\n[00:43.31]\n[00:43.99]What it all comes down to\n[00:46.62]\n[00:51.43]One by one\n[00:54.49]The lonely feelings come\n[00:56.43]\n[00:57.68]Day by day  they slowly fade away\n[01:04.56]\n[01:05.50]Ooh  the look was in her eyes\n[01:09.00]\n[01:09.56]You never know what might be found there\n[01:12.80]\n[01:15.74]She was dancing right in time\n[01:19.05]And the looks she made so fine\n[01:22.11]Like the music that surrounds her\n[01:26.06]\n[01:29.88]Should I stay or go\n[01:32.75]\n[01:33.25]I really want to know\n[01:36.19]Would I loose or win\n[01:39.19]If I try and love again\n[01:41.56]\n[01:48.68]Gonna try and love again\n[01:51.37]\n[02:00.81]I\'m gonna try and love again\n[02:03.74]\n[02:13.42]Gonna try and love\n[02:17.48]\n[02:40.23]Right or wrong  what\'s done is done\n[02:44.42]It\'s only moments that we borrow\n[02:47.94]\n[02:50.94]But the thoughts will linger on\n[02:53.94]Of the lady and her song\n[02:56.32]\n[02:57.00]When the sun comes up tomorrow\n[03:00.77]\n[03:05.02]Well  it might take years to see\n[03:08.72]Through all these tears\n[03:11.47]Don\'t let go\n[03:14.16]When you find it you will know\n[03:16.97]\n[03:19.22]Oh  Gonna try and love again\n[03:26.60]\n[03:36.01]Gonna try and love again\n[03:39.20]\n[03:48.33]Gonna try and love again\n[03:50.82]\n[04:02.77]Sometimes lose  sometimes win\n[04:05.45]Sometimes you need a friend\n[04:07.38]\n[04:20.88]Gonna try  gonna try\n[04:30.57]\n[04:32.74]Gonna try  gonna try','311.12','原声带,欧美流行','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songCovers/f83456ec-e68d-4242-b132-d13f00da8fb4-Eagles-Try and Love Again (2013 Remaster).jpg','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songs/ad18b76b-c008-470e-8ebd-1b3cb02f54d8-Eagles - Try and Love Again (2013 Remaster).mp3','2026-04-16'),(636,155,'Waiting in the Weeds','Long Road out of Eden','{\"t\":0,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作词: \"},{\"tx\":\"Don Henley\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Steuart Smith\"}]}\n{\"t\":1000,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作曲: \"},{\"tx\":\"Don Henley\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Steuart Smith\"}]}\n[00:11.66]It\'s comin\'on the end of August\n[00:20.66]Another summer\'s promise almost gone\n[00:30.63]And though I heard some wise man say\n[00:35.97]That every dog will have his day\n[00:41.17]He never mentioned that these dog days get so long\n[00:51.72]I don\'t know when I realized the dream was over\n[01:02.19]Well, there was no particular h