4.300]Just nod if you can hear me.\n[00:18.300]Is there anyone home?\n[00:22.300]Come on, now.\n[00:25.300]I hear you\'re feeling down.\n[00:29.300]Well I can ease your pain,\n[00:33.299]Get you on your feet again.\n[00:38.299]Relax.\n[00:40.299]I need some information first.\n[00:45.299]Just the basic facts:\n[00:48.299]Can you show me where it hurts?\n[00:53.299]There is no pain, you are receding.\n[01:00.899]A distant ship\'s smoke on the horizon.\n[01:09.899]You are only coming through in waves.\n[01:16.899]Your lips move but I can\'t hear what you\'re saying\n[01:22.899]When I was a child I had a fever.\n[01:30.899]My hands felt just like two balloons.\n[01:38.899]Now I got that feeling once again.\n[01:43.899]I can\'t explain, you would not understand.\n[01:48.899]This is not how I am.\n[01:56.390]I have become comfortably numb.\n[02:47.500]Ok.\n[02:50.500]Just a little pinprick.\n[02:54.500]There\'ll be no more --Aaaaaahhhhh!\n[02:58.500]But you may feel a little sick.\n[03:02.500]Can you stand up?\n[03:05.500]I do believe it\'s working. Good.\n[03:09.500]That\'ll keep you going  through the show.\n[03:13.500]Come on it\'s time to go.\n[03:18.500]There is no pain, you are receding.\n[03:25.500]A distant ship\'s smoke on the horizon.\n[03:33.500]You are only coming through in waves.\n[03:40.500]Your lips move but I can\'t hear what you\'re sayin\'.\n[03:48.500]When I was a child I caught a fleeting glimpse,\n[03:56.500]Out of the corner of my eye.\n[04:03.500]I turned to look but it was gone.\n[04:08.500]I cannot put my finger on it now.\n[04:12.500]The child is grown, the dream is gone.\n[04:18.500]I have become comfortably numb.','382.04','欧美流行','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songCovers/5641e2b8-5a21-41aa-91a6-8e13c06c6c67-Pink Floyd-Comfortably Numb.jpg','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songs/b6f97a43-f51d-40a8-b2b5-5ee7c595df05-Pink Floyd - Comfortably Numb.mp3','2026-04-16'),(689,174,'Echoes','Meddle','[02:57.72]Overhead the albatross\n[03:01.20]Hangs motionless upon the air\n[03:05.01]And deep beneath the rolling waves\n[03:08.91]In labyrinths of coral caves\n[03:12.99]The echo of a distant time\n[03:16.63]Comes willowing across the sand\n[03:20.22]And everything is green and submarine\n[03:28.03]And no one showed us to the land\n[03:31.70]And no one knows the where\'s or why\'s\n[03:35.46]Something stirs and something tries\n[03:38.96]And starts to climb toward the light\n[03:45.17]\n[04:11.77]Strangers passing in the street\n[04:15.28]By chance two separate glances meet\n[04:18.89]And I am you and what I see is me\n[04:26.61]And do I take you by the hand\n[04:30.85]And lead you through the land\n[04:33.78]And help me understand the best I can\n[04:41.28]And no one calls us to move on\n[04:44.53]And no one forces down our eyes\n[04:48.52]No one speaks and no one tries\n[04:52.21]No one flies around the sun\n[04:58.22]\n[19:11.47]Cloudless everyday you fall\n[19:14.94]Upon my waking eyes\n[19:18.61]Inviting and inciting me\n[19:22.30]To rise\n[19:26.19]And through the window in the wall\n[19:29.73]Come streaming in on sunlight wings\n[19:33.51]A million bright ambassadors of morning\n[19:40.74]And no one sings me lullabies\n[19:44.70]And no one makes me close my eyes\n[19:48.39]So I throw the windows wide\n[19:52.02]And call to you across the sky','1411.58','欧美流行','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songCovers/d128047b-0f06-402b-8946-90256573ffc0-Pink Floyd-Echoes.jpg','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songs/46e845ab-cbde-4b84-8620-a79969bb8855-Pink Floyd - Echoes.mp3','2026-04-16'),(690,174,'Fearless','Meddle','{\"t\":0,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作词: \"},{\"tx\":\"Pink Floyd\"}]}\n{\"t\":1000,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作曲: \"},{\"tx\":\"Pink Floyd\"}]}\n[00:44.30]You say the hill\'s too steep to climb\n[00:51.41]Climb it\n[00:57.77]You say you\'d like to see me try\n[01:04.74]Climbing\n[01:11.05]You pick the place and I\'ll choose the time\n[01:16.71]And I\'ll climb\n[01:19.43]That hill in my own way\n[01:24.73]Just wait a while for the right day\n[01:32.11]And as I rise above the tree lines and the clouds\n[01:37.81]I look down hearing the sound of the things you\'ve said today\n[01:46.64]\n[02:47.30]Fearlessly the idiot faced the crowd\n[02:54.81]Smiling\n[03:00.83]Merciless the magistrate turns around\n[03:08.46]Frowning\n[03:14.68]And who\'s the fool who wears the crown\n[03:20.69]And go down\n[03:23.39]In your own way\n[03:28.80]And every day is the right day\n[03:36.09]And as you rise above the fear-lines in his brow\n[03:41.87]You look down hearing the sound of the faces in the crowd','367.93','欧美流行','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songCovers/8273c139-5bec-4fa7-baf9-723df31ba27c-Pink Floyd-Fearless.jpg','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songs/4c561f6a-f149-48b6-94d6-9717907719ec-Pink Floyd - Fearless.mp3','2026-04-16'),(691,174,'Green is the Colour','More','{\"t\":0,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作词: \"},{\"tx\":\"Roger Waters\"}]}\n{\"t\":1000,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作曲: \"},{\"tx\":\"Roger Waters\"}]}\n[00:26.774]Heavy  hung  the  canopy  of  blue\n[00:33.69]Shade  my  eyes  and  I  can  see  you\n[00:39.815]White  is  the  light  that  shines  through  the  dress  that  you  wore\n[00:52.57]She  lay  in  the  shadow  of  the  wave\n[00:58.782]Hazy  were  the  visions  overplayed\n[01:05.88]Sunlight  in  her  eyes  but  moonshine  made  her  blind  every  time\n[01:18.239]Green  is  the  colour  of  her  kind\n[01:24.592]Quickness  of  the  eye  deceives  the  mind\n[01:30.673]Envy  is  the  bond  between  the  hopeful  and  the  damned','178.83','欧美流行','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songCovers/18b4cdb8-5005-4b50-9f22-bccbcd1eda8a-Pink Floyd-Green is the Colour.jpg','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songs/7d3c2194-a5b1-41bb-a071-413785ed0c78-Pink Floyd - Green is the Colour.mp3','2026-04-16'),(692,174,'If','Atom Heart Mother','{\"t\":0,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作词: \"},{\"tx\":\"Roger Waters\"}]}\n{\"t\":1000,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作曲: \"},{\"tx\":\"Roger Waters\"}]}\n[00:09.02]If I were a swan, I\'d be gone.\n[00:20.10]If I were a train, I\'d be late.\n[00:28.53]And if I were a good man, I\'d talk with you, more often than I do.\n[00:46.78]If I were to sleep, I could dream.\n[00:56.99]If I were afraid, I could hide.\n[01:06.22]If I go insane, please don\'t put your wires in my brain.\n[02:02.52]If I were the moon, I\'d be cool.\n[02:11.63]If I were a rule, I would bend.\n[02:21.04]If I were a good man, I\'d understand the spaces between friends\n[02:39.59]If I were alone, I would cry.\n[02:48.62]And if I were with you, I\'d be home and dry.\n[02:57.90]And if I go insane, will you still let me join in with the game?\n[03:54.05]If I were a swan, I\'d be gone.\n[04:03.49]If I were a train, I\'d be late again.\n[04:12.48]If I were a good man, I\'d talk with you, more often than I do.','270.77','欧美流行','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songCovers/1d9d25ae-09a9-430f-9050-82598ab899f1-Pink Floyd-If.jpg','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songs/a4a64518-204f-4b55-94a4-85a9176fc115-Pink Floyd - If.mp3','2026-04-16'),(693,174,'San Tropez','Meddle','{\"t\":0,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作词: \"},{\"tx\":\"Roger Waters\"}]}\n{\"t\":1000,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作曲: \"},{\"tx\":\"Roger Waters\"}]}\n[00:04.27]As I reach for a peach\n[00:06.45]Slide a rind down behind\n[00:08.85]The sofa in San Tropez\n[00:15.40]Breaking a stick with a brick on the sand\n[00:19.46]Riding a wave in the wake of an old Sedan\n[00:27.46]Sleeping alone in the drone of the darkness\n[00:31.68]Scratched by the sand that fell from our love\n[00:35.50]Deep in my dreams and I still hear her calling\n[00:39.84]If you\'re alone I\'ll come home\n[00:43.52]Backwards and home bound\n[00:45.36]The pidgeon the dove\n[00:47.62]Gone with the wind and the rain on an airplane\n[00:51.83]Owning a home with no silver spoon\n[00:55.44]I\'m drinking champaigne like a big tycoon\n[00:59.52]Sooner than wait for a break in the weather\n[01:03.39]I\'ll gather my far flung thoughts together\n[01:07.41]Speeding away on a wind to a new day\n[01:11.31]If your alone I\'ll come home\n[01:15.00]\n[01:46.40]And I pause for a while\n[01:48.47]By a country style\n[01:50.76]And listen to things they say\n[01:57.03]Digging for gold in the hoe in my hand\n[02:00.88]Hoping they\'ll take a look at the way things stand\n[02:08.05]And you\'re leading me down to the place by the sea\n[02:12.47]I hear your soft voice calling to me\n[02:16.49]Making a date for later by phone\n[02:20.38]If you\'re alone I\'ll come home','223.03','欧美流行','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songCovers/2de49b3a-1884-43c7-9b95-66392107b427-Pink Floyd-San Tropez.jpg','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songs/197aa56b-5f2c-4a0e-95ae-4debda136d94-Pink Floyd - San Tropez.mp3','2026-04-16'),(694,174,'Stay','Obscured by Clouds','{\"t\":0,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作词: \"},{\"tx\":\"Roger Waters\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Richard Wright\"}]}\n{\"t\":1000,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作曲: \"},{\"tx\":\"Roger Waters\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Richard Wright\"}]}\n[00:35.48]Stay and help me to end the day.\n[00:43.07]And if you don\'t mind,\n[00:47.62]We\'ll break a bottle of wine.\n[00:52.04]Stick around and maybe we\'ll put one down,\n[01:00.29]Because I wanna find what lies behind those eyes.\n[01:10.51]Midnight blue burning gold.\n[01:18.84]A yellow moon is growing cold.\n[01:43.02]I rise, looking through my morning eyes,\n[01:51.41]Surprised to find you by my side.\n[01:59.61]Rack my brain to try to remember your name\n[02:08.22]To find the words to tell you good-bye.\n[02:17.68]Morning dues.\n[02:18.77]\n[02:21.80]Newborn day.\n[02:25.76]Midnight blue turned to gray.\n[03:14.72]Midnight blue burning gold.\n[03:22.43]A yellow moon is growing cold.','247.25','欧美流行','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songCovers/c752602e-0c39-4588-9b27-06458101f4fd-Pink Floyd-Stay.jpg','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songs/7ae6ae4a-2678-4135-b4e8-41299905dbe1-Pink Floyd - Stay.mp3','2026-04-16'),(695,174,'The Great Gig in the Sky','The Dark Side of the Moon','{\"t\":0,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作词: \"},{\"tx\":\"Wright\"}]}\n{\"t\":1000,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作曲: \"},{\"tx\":\"Clare\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Torry\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Richard\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Wright\"}]}\n[00:03.74]Music：Wright\n[00:05.12]Vocal：Clare Torry\n[00:38.96]\n[00:39.15]\'And I am not frightened of dying, any time will do,\n[00:42.74]I don\'t mind. Why should I be frightened of dying?\n[00:49.68]There\'s no reason for it, you\'ve gotta go sometime.\'\n[03:30.54]\n[03:33.88]\'I never said I was frightened of dying.\'','283.64','欧美流行','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songCovers/18baaae7-e247-48c4-a62d-36d8be51ceac-Pink Floyd-The Great Gig in the Sky.jpg','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songs/c10203a8-957b-491e-8243-d690b321c064-Pink Floyd - The Great Gig in the Sky.mp3','2026-04-16'),(696,174,'Time','The Dark Side of the Moon','{\"t\":0,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作词: \"},{\"tx\":\"Waters\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Roger\"}]}\n{\"t\":1000,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作曲: \"},{\"tx\":\"Mason\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"David\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Gilmour\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Waters\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Richard\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Roger\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Wright\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Nick\"}]}\n[02:14.74]Ticking away the moments that make up a dull day\n[02:21.97]You fritter and waste the hours in an offhand way\n[02:29.40]Kicking around on a piece of ground in your home town\n[02:36.55]Waiting for someone or something to show you the way\n[02:41.74]\n[02:43.83]Tired of lying in the sunshine staying home to watch the rain\n[02:51.39]You are young and life is long and there is time to kill today\n[02:59.27]And then one day you find ten years have got behind you\n[03:06.49]No one told you when to run, you missed the starting gun\n[03:14.41]\n[04:40.55]And you run and you run to catch up with the sun, but it\'s sinking\n[04:48.33]And racing around to come up behind you again\n[04:55.35]The sun is the same in the relative way, but you\'re older\n[05:02.37]Shorter of breath and one day closer to death\n[05:06.95]\n[05:09.54]Every year is getting shorter, never seem to find the time\n[05:16.82]Plans that either come to naught or half a page of scribbled lines\n[05:24.35]Hanging on in quiet desperation is the English way\n[05:31.56]The time is gone the song is over, thought I\'d something more to say\n[05:39.78]\n[05:56.91]Home, home again\n[06:04.19]I like to be here when I can\n[06:12.10]And when I come home cold and tired\n[06:19.13]It\'s good to warm my bones beside the fire\n[06:27.09]Far away across the field\n[06:31.07]The tolling of the iron bell\n[06:35.26]Calls the faithful to their knees\n[06:39.27]To hear the softly spoken magic spells.','413.78','欧美流行','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songCovers/5a564eeb-4117-4d90-bfe5-dbc22f02cb67-Pink Floyd-Time.jpg','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songs/3690c31f-7d6d-41c2-87c1-009552fae8b0-Pink Floyd - Time.mp3','2026-04-16'),(697,174,'Us and Them','The Dark Side of the Moon','{\"t\":0,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作词: \"},{\"tx\":\"Waters\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Roger\"}]}\n{\"t\":1000,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作曲: \"},{\"tx\":\"Waters\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Richard\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Roger\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Wright\"}]}\n[00:16.627]\n[01:42.492]Us and Them\n[01:57.591]And after all we\'re only ordinary men\n[02:16.268]Me, and you\n[02:31.158]God only knows it\'s not what we would choose to do\n[02:49.862]\"Forward!\" he cried from the rear\n[02:54.381]and the front rank died\n[03:02.766]And the General sat, and the lines on the map\n[03:09.140]moved from side to side\n[03:13.476]\n[03:15.906]Black and Blue\n[03:30.299]And who knows which is which and who is who\n[03:49.264]Up and Down\n[04:03.971]And in the end it\'s only round and round and round\n[04:22.283]\"Haven\'t you heard it\'s a battle of words\"\n[04:27.925]the poster bearer cried\n[04:34.978]\"Listen son,\" said the man with the gun\n[04:40.882]\"There\'s room for you inside\"\n[04:45.166]\n[06:19.181]Down and Out\n[06:33.600]It can\'t be helped but there\'s a lot of it about\n[06:52.226]With, without\n[07:06.567]And who\'ll deny that\'s what the fightings all about\n[07:25.323]\"Get out of the way, it\'s a busy day\n[07:30.391]And I\'ve got things on my mind\"\n[07:37.104]For want of the price of tea and a slice\n[07:43.243]The old man died','469.21','欧美流行','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songCovers/14d55803-2838-4e8a-89b2-4da85e61c59d-Pink Floyd-Us and Them.jpg','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songs/f9b3ce1f-57bf-409f-b6d2-c4f65fcacd01-Pink Floyd - Us and Them.mp3','2026-04-16'),(698,174,'Wish You Were Here','Wish You Were Here','{\"t\":0,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作词: \"},{\"tx\":\"Roger Waters\"}]}\n{\"t\":1000,\"c\":[{\"tx\":\"作曲: \"},{\"tx\":\"David Gilmour\"},{\"tx\":\"/\"},{\"tx\":\"Roger Waters\"}]}\n[01:35.320]So\n[01:37.390]So you think you can tell\n[01:42.340]Heaven from Hell\n[01:45.780]Blue skies from pain\n[01:50.100]Can you tell a green field\n[01:54.350]From a cold steel rail?\n[01:58.770]A smile from a veil?\n[02:02.780]Do you think you can tell?\n[02:06.810]And did they get you to trade\n[02:10.980]Your heroes for ghosts?\n[02:15.090]Hot ashes for trees?\n[02:19.140]Hot air for a cool breeze?\n[02:23.120]Cold comfort for change?\n[02:27.320]And did you exchange\n[02:31.000]A walk on part in the war\n[02:34.290]For a lead role in a cage?\n[03:16.990]How I wish\n[03:19.000]How I wish you were here\n[03:23.670]We\'re just two lost souls swimming in a fish bowl\n[03:28.890]Year after year\n[03:32.790]Running over the same old ground\n[03:36.830]What have we found?\n[03:39.330]The same old fears\n[03:42.860]Wish you were here','334.68','原声带,欧美流行','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songCovers/77e66d9b-2196-4227-b20b-6a0dfd1ca54c-Pink Floyd-Wish You Were Here.jpg','http://127.0.0.1:9000/vibe-music-data/songs/a47a76b0-0bd5-41ad-80f1-d7c2f571a0d1-Pink Floyd - Wish You We